 excluded when looking for multiplicative inverses in $\\mathbb{R}$?","options":["Because multiplication is not a binary operation on $\\mathbb{R}$.","Because $0$ is not a real number.","There is no real number $b$ with $0\\cdot b=1$.","Because $0$ has two different inverses."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ee33f9c5a8c0151ca95079bd","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch20_inverse_element_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For $a\\star b=a+b+1$ on $\\mathbb{R}$, the identity is $-1$. What is the inverse of $a$?","options":["$1/a$","$-a-2$","$-a$","$-a-1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"faee6647e342d597a748dcf9","time_limit":25},{"id":"la_batch20_inverse_element_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"If every element of a monoid has an inverse, what kind of structure is obtained?","options":["A group.","A binary operation that is not closed.","A semigroup with no identity.","A vector space automatically."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5869adf7c5f03c975b6b49ec","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch20_inverse_element_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why can the same element have different inverses under different operations?","options":["The inverse is always the reciprocal, just written differently.","The inverse never depends on the identity element.","Changing the operation changes the set, so the element changes.","Both identity and inverse equation depend on the operation."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"000c1069ffe8b194524ef4ec","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch20_inverse_element_016","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"In addition modulo $5$, what is the inverse of $3$?","options":["$2$","$3$","$1$","$0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"79c4aa20435487c8bebe02ef","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch20_inverse_element_006_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"In a group $(G,\\star)$, which element is always the inverse of $a\\star b$?","options":["$b^{-1}\\star a^{-1}$","$a^{-1}\\star b^{-1}$","$a^{-1}\\star b$","$b\\star a$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1bcc741997572a5b2bfd1fba","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch20_inverse_element_010_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"In $\\mathbb{Z}$ under multiplication, with identity $1$, which integers $a$ have an inverse in $\\mathbb{Z}$?","options":["Only $1$ and $-1$","Every nonzero integer, with inverse $1/a$","Only $1$, since it is the identity","None, since $(\\mathbb{Z},\\cdot)$ is not a group"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c6fdf5fc2db2e5167dd66f78","time_limit":30}]}}